s4-5-p2 : Block
s4-5-p2 = prose (cons "The equations of §§3–4 say what each computation returns. They leave to their reader the act of substituting, the choice of where to reduce, and what becomes of a value used twice or not yet known. With interaction as the only primitive there is no such reader: the same rules are stated here as interactions, and nothing is left outside them. A term is a net of cells. Every cell has one principal port and some other ports. A value is a cell that offers itself at its principal port: a λ, a pair, a type, a constructor, an interval point, a system. An operation is a cell that wants one value at its principal port: application, the projections, path application, composition, case, substitution, duplication, erasure. A wire connects two ports; a wire may be empty for a time, the first side to arrive leaving what it has and the second finding it. An active pair is an operation's principal port wired to a value's principal port. A step removes the two cells of an active pair and puts in their place a small net on the wires they held. No rule consults anything but the two cells that met. Two values wired together, or two operations wired together, do nothing." nil)
